      {
         "id": "SECTION_introduction",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "<p><h3>The Most Spoken Language</h3>We can consider mathematics as the language of nature; in this way, it is present everywhere.</p><p>As we study mathematics, we come to understand how nature works. With this knowledge, we can create, among other things, the electronic device you are using to learn.</p><p>In this lesson, we will see that humanity has been learning the language of nature, with mistakes and successes that help us understand the universe.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_inus",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "<p><h3>In Us</h3>We have already seen that we can use numbers with our hands, but not only that. Look below: we can also number different parts of our body with them.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><img id=\"imgHumanBody\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgHumanBody', '0%')\" class=\"imgcenter\"/><b>Figure 1</b>: Human body with its numbered parts.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_intexts",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "<p><h3>In Our Texts</h3>One of the places where numbers are present is in texts. For example, we can count the letters and the words we are reading. Moreover, there are texts that do not use the alphabet; they use hieroglyphs, like the stela at Copán, Honduras. We can also count these hieroglyphs.</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 0,
                     "uuid": "1e007481-9bd3-4a09-ad4d-6e812fe79641",
                     "text": "Instituto Hondureño de Antropologia e Historia",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "02",
                        "day": "01"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "5390fa3b-735f-4e22-ac98-178303a13fdb",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Writing",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><img id=\"imgCopanText\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgCopanText', '0%')\" class=\"imgcenter\"/><b>Figure 2</b>: Stela, altar and hieroglyphs in the form of a staircase at Copán, Honduras (<htcite0>).</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 0,
                     "uuid": "1e007481-9bd3-4a09-ad4d-6e812fe79641",
                     "text": "Instituto Hondureño de Antropologia e Historia",
