      {
         "id": "SECTION_ages",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "<p><h3>Ages</h3>Our knowledge about the past of humanity, of the planet and of the universe is something new. But this does not mean that, before, we did not try to explain it in a poetic way.</p><p>For example, the Sumerian King List, which contains real kings and others never proven to have existed, says that, in different cities, there were 8 kings who, together, ruled for 241,200 years, with one of them ruling for 43,200 years (<htcite0> ; <htcite1> ; <htcite2>).</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 0,
                     "uuid": "cb216fdf-1282-42e0-aaf4-3547b53857d7",
                     "text": "Black, J.A. et al.",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "1998",
                        "month": "04",
                        "day": "16"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 0,
                     "uuid": "c8dd380c-6f66-415c-94fa-b116308adeef",
                     "text": "Black, J.A. et al.",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "1998",
                        "month": "04",
                        "day": "16"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "376a5f3c-c598-40ee-95ad-5db9046ab8e2",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Sumerians - The Mythological Kings",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><img id=\"imgKingList\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgKingList', '0%')\" class=\"imgcenter\"/><b>Figure 3</b>: Sumerian King List. © Ashmolean Museum, University of Oxford (<htcite0>).</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "376a5f3c-c598-40ee-95ad-5db9046ab8e2",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Sumerians - The Mythological Kings",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p>The Sumerian King List attributes periods of rule of millennia - more than a thousand years - to some people. As we move through the texts, we see that this period gradually reduces to centuries - periods of more than 100 years - and, finally, reaches the periods of time we live today.</p><p>Would it be possible for people to have lived for centuries or millennia, as the Sumerians wrote and other peoples possibly learned from them?</p><p><b>Answer:</b> no. The lifespan of people in the past was not different from today's.</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 0,
                     "uuid": "cb216fdf-1282-42e0-aaf4-3547b53857d7",
                     "text": "Black, J.A. et al.",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "1998",
                        "month": "04",
                        "day": "16"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 0,
                     "uuid": "c8dd380c-6f66-415c-94fa-b116308adeef",
                     "text": "Black, J.A. et al.",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "1998",
                        "month": "04",
                        "day": "16"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "376a5f3c-c598-40ee-95ad-5db9046ab8e2",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Sumerians - The Mythological Kings",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_wrongright",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "<p><h3>Wrong, but Right</h3>When the Sumerians proposed that a few kings had ruled for more than 200,000 years, they wrote something impossible; after all, the lifespan of people in the past was not different from today's.</p><p>On the other hand, even without having the necessary knowledge, they managed to conclude that humanity does not have a short history.</p><p>Today, we know that several human species existed and that, possibly, others are still to be discovered (<htcite0> ; <htcite1> ; <htcite2>).</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "7fa66cfd-dca8-4a17-bead-e79954ba684a",
                     "text": "Wood, B., & Collard, M.",
                     "page": "pp. 65",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "1999",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "f4f9c247-4a7e-4277-8691-99659cf2c240",
                     "text": "Cy",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2021",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
